{"ts":"2026-09-08T07:24:15.421538975Z","session":"3e77d415-4373-4de0-87c3-8da6e98363dc","agent_type":"bwk","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"git add cmd/ethos/mission.go internal/mcp/mission_tools.go cmd/ethos/mission_test.go internal/mcp/mission_tools_test.go \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nfix(mission): name actual queue position at dispatch time, not an assumed one (K8)\n\nReview finding K8 (full-branch review, m-2026-09-08-004 round 3),\nMEDIUM: bindDispatchedMission's advisory line (CLI and MCP) claimed\nunconditionally that worker's NEXT matching Agent() spawn goes to the\nmission just dispatched -- false whenever an OLDER pending dispatch for\nthe same worker is already queued, since FIFO always matches the oldest\nfirst. matchDispatchPending's own ambiguity warning fires correctly at\nSPAWN time; this message was wrong at DISPATCH time, the moment the\nleader actually reads it.\n\nBoth call sites now read the pending-dispatch store back after writing\ntheir own entry and report its actual queue position: first in line\nkeeps the original \"will attribute worker's next matching spawn\"\nwording; queued behind an older entry gets a wording naming what is\nahead of it and that FIFO will match the older one first. A read\nfailure falls back to the original wording rather than blocking or\nsilencing the advisory -- this line is best-effort visibility, never a\ngate.\n\nTwo regression tests (CLI, MCP) drive two back-to-back same-worker\ndispatches/creates and assert the second names the first mission as\nahead of it, confirmed failing against pre-fix code via git-stash\nfalsification.\nEOF\n)\""},"tool_input_hash":"5b101504a50da3196960eb0f605725d23823bfc1ff3a02a31648c915508da865","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"git add cmd/ethos/mission.go internal/mcp/mission_tools.go cmd/ethos/mission_test.go internal/mcp/mission_tools_test.go \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nfix(mission): ..."}
